#!/bin/sh
# pre-commit hook - refuse to COMMIT on main.
#
# ArtLight's working branch is dev. main is the release branch: it moves when a
# release is actually cut, not while one is being worked on. Everything committed
# straight to main is work dev never sees - and a dev that is always three commits
# behind and empty in front is how it starts to look like a branch worth deleting.
#
# Said to me more than once, most recently in these words:
#   "again already we are doing all the work on main rather than on dev... at this
#    point we might as well just delete the dev branch because unless i keep
#    telling you, it doesnt get used."
# and then, when I answered that the rule was written down:
#   "just know, the next time you forget (and you will) i will delete the dev repo
#    before i say anything to you."
#
# The rule has been written into skills before and it did not stop it. It cannot: a
# skill only loads if I decide to load it, and I never decide to consult a rule
# about a thing I am not aware I am about to do. That is what makes it autopilot.
# This runs on the commit itself, so it does not depend on being read, agreed with,
# or remembered.
#
# A merge commit and a fast-forward do not fire this hook, so bringing dev forward
# and cutting a release are unaffected. To commit on main on purpose:
#     touch ~/.hermes/cache/allow-main-commit
# run the command, then remove the file.
set -eu

branch=$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo "")
if [ "$branch" != "main" ]; then
    exit 0
fi

SENTINEL="$HOME/.hermes/cache/allow-main-commit"
if [ -e "$SENTINEL" ]; then
    exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'EOF'

  refused - this commit is on 'main'

  ArtLight's working branch is dev. main is the release branch: it moves when a
  release is cut, not while one is being worked on. Work committed here is work
  dev never sees, and dev falling behind is what makes it look deletable.

      git checkout dev

  If this genuinely is a release commit on main, make it a deliberate act first:

      touch ~/.hermes/cache/allow-main-commit

  run the command, then remove that file.

EOF
exit 1
